# Keeps `public/` in the repository.
#
# Next.js serves this directory as static assets, and frontend/Dockerfile:44
# does `COPY --from=builder /app/public ./public`, which fails the whole image
# build if the directory is absent. Git does not track empty directories, so
# without a file in here the build works only on machines where the folder
# happens to exist and fails on every fresh clone.
#
# Delete this once there is a real asset alongside it.
